WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:09.800
Vina spent her first year mastering the team's reporting tool.

2
00:00:09.800 --> 00:00:17.500
On Monday morning the team hears that from March, a new AI tool will replace it.

3
00:00:17.500 --> 00:00:25.600
Her first thought: a year wasted. Her second: they are replacing us. Neither is a fact yet.

4
00:00:25.600 --> 00:00:34.600
Look at what she really learned that year. Above ground are the tools: a spreadsheet, a dashboard, a reporting system.

5
00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:41.500
Below ground are the fundamentals: logic, statistics, clear writing, and judgement about her field.

6
00:00:41.500 --> 00:00:49.600
Tools are replaced every few years. The fundamentals carry over to each new one, and they compound.

7
00:00:49.600 --> 00:00:57.300
So for anything you learn, ask: which part of this survives when the tool is replaced?

8
00:00:57.300 --> 00:01:03.000
To keep the fundamentals growing, she sets up a small loop.

9
00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:07.100
One source she trusts and really reads.

10
00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:12.000
One small project where she uses what she read.

11
00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:18.900
One log: a line each week on what she tried and what she learned.

12
00:01:18.900 --> 00:01:27.800
And one defended hour a week. A logged hour beats a panic sprint every time a new tool trends.

13
00:01:27.800 --> 00:01:36.800
A skill nobody can see is invisible to those who could reward it. So Vina lists hers, with the public proof beside each one.

14
00:01:36.800 --> 00:01:42.500
Analysis: a project with the workings shown. Writing: two published articles.

15
00:01:42.500 --> 00:01:47.400
Presenting: nothing yet. That gap is her next project.

16
00:01:47.400 --> 00:01:56.400
Back to Monday. Before she reacts, Vina pauses and separates fact from interpretation. They are replacing us is an interpretation.

17
00:01:56.400 --> 00:02:03.300
The fact is one sentence: the team will use the new tool from March.

18
00:02:03.300 --> 00:02:10.200
Then she chooses one action inside her control: she asks to join the pilot.

19
00:02:10.200 --> 00:02:19.200
A senior colleague says the last new system failed too. Vina does not argue. She asks: what went wrong that time?

20
00:02:19.200 --> 00:02:28.200
Questions bring the real concern to the surface. People accept a change more readily when they have had a voice in it.

21
00:02:28.200 --> 00:02:31.200
Tools expire. Fundamentals compound.

22
00:02:31.200 --> 00:02:36.100
One logged hour a week beats a panic sprint.

23
00:02:36.100 --> 00:02:45.100
Now it is your turn. Name one fundamental in your field, and one place where you will show it publicly.
